# Extend before invent

Applies to new or changed documentation under this framework.

**Mantra:** simple, consistent, reusable. Do not invent a parallel structure when the standard already has a home.

## Default workflow

1. **Find the sibling** — search `docs/en/templates/`, category hubs, and `examples/` for the same grain (overview, contract, runbook, ADR, security asset, etc.).
2. **Cite the reference** — name the template or example path in the reply/PR.
3. **Extend or mirror** — copy the section layout and metadata conventions; adapt content only.
4. **New structure only when no sibling exists** — justify in chat and document why in the nearest README the same session.

| Need | Start here |
| --- | --- |
| Project / system overview | `docs/en/templates/project-overview.md` |
| Architecture | [architecture-model.md](docs/en/architecture-model.md) + architecture templates |
| Contracts | [contract-model.md](docs/en/contract-model.md) + `docs/en/templates/contract.md` |
| Operations | [operations-model.md](docs/en/operations-model.md) + ops templates |
| Security | [security-model.md](docs/en/security-model.md) + security templates |
| AI-ready context | [ai-context.md](docs/en/ai-context.md), [ai-ready-model.md](docs/en/ai-ready-model.md) |
| Agent entry files | [ai-agent-entry.md](docs/en/ai-agent-entry.md), `examples/adopter-agent-starter/` |
| Adoption path | [adoption-path.md](docs/en/adoption-path.md), `examples/adoption-scaffold/` |

## Complexity gate

If the proposed doc layout is **more complex** than the sibling (new category, custom taxonomy, extra metadata schemes): tell the user **before writing** — what, why no simpler path, and how it maps to existing hubs.

## Anti-patterns

- New top-level doc trees that bypass `docs/en/` / `docs/pt-BR/`
- One-off heading schemes that break progressive disclosure
- Copying an unrelated domain's structure because names look similar

